# Git & GitHub — businessfunding

## Commit identity

- Always commit as **John Pastre** `<john@ollacart.com>`.
- Use the repo-local git config (`user.name`, `user.email`) — do not change global git config.
- Push to **https://github.com/OllaCart/businessfunding.git** using the **OllaCart** GitHub account.

## No Cursor attribution

- Never add `Co-authored-by: Cursor` or any Cursor agent attribution to commit messages.
- Keep commit messages professional and focused on the change only.

## Example commit

```bash
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Short summary of the change.

Optional one-sentence explanation of why.
EOF
)"
```
